# ROSA HCP on AWS 759945100724 (OCM stage) — SUCCESS
# Date: 2026-10-12

Working ROSA HCP cluster created end to end. This directory supersedes the
flat hcp/01-..05-* files, which record the earlier attempt on account
301721915996 that was blocked at OCM org <-> AWS account authorization.

## What was different this time

The blocker was never the OCM org (Red Hat1, 1HAXGgCYqHpednsRDiwWsZBmDlA --
same org both times) and never the Red Hat SSO login. It was the AWS account:
301721915996 had no ocm-role linked to Red Hat1, and its only ocm-role was a
shared CI role we would not touch.

759945100724 is empty and dedicated, so `rosa create ocm-role` (step 01) could
create AND link our own role. Everything after that just worked.

